<title>TAIWAN: Acer up after buying TI unit.</title>
<headline>Acer up after buying TI unit.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>shares of Taiwan's computer giant Acer Inc surged in early Friday trade on news that the company had bought the notebook computer business of U.S.-based Texas Instruments, brokers said.</p>
<p>After 45 minutes, Acer rose T$2.0 or 4.0 percent to T$52, while the overall index rose 0.89 percent.</p>
</text>
